<html><body>
<p>Hello everyone,</p>

<p>The Executive Leadership Committee approved two updated policies that take effect on <b>January 1, 2026</b>. Both are posted in the canonical policy folder on the HR share, and those documents are the official versions. Here are the highlights.</p>

<h3>Travel and Business Expense Policy (HR-214, version 4.0)</h3>
<ul>
<li>Per diem goes up to $65 per day, or $85 in high-cost locations.</li>
<li>Hotel caps go up to $210 per night, or $290 in high-cost locations.</li>
<li>Mileage is now 62 cents per mile.</li>
<li>You only need a receipt for expenses of $30 or more.</li>
<li>Expense reports are due within 30 days. This is shorter than before, so please plan for it.</li>
<li>Managers approve reports up to $500. Department heads also approve reports above $500, and the CFO approves anything over $2,500.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Remote and Hybrid Work Policy (HR-220, version 2.0)</h3>
<ul>
<li>New fully remote arrangement for eligible roles, with a one-time home office allowance of up to $400.</li>
<li>The connectivity stipend increases to $50 per month for hybrid and fully remote employees.</li>
<li>If the Credit Union needs to change or end an arrangement, you will get at least 30 days' written notice.</li>
<li>Hybrid employees continue to work in the office at least two days a week.</li>
</ul>

<p>Managers will receive a short briefing pack next week. Handbook sections and team wiki pages will be updated in January.</p>

<p>Thank you,<br>
Human Resources</p>
